lisa-design:
docs-review-verify mounts the docs repo as a ro repo item (=task.target.repo + '@main'): checkout: read-only plus repos mounts only the repo items (planMounts), without the task repo. The review skill checks out the PR head in its own workspace.
The up script adds what a fresh local-dev clone needs in the VM: .env from .env.example (the Makefile includes it), COMPOSE_COMMAND="docker compose" (default podman-compose), CCF_IMAGES=file when a version is set (latest would replace the pins), and one retry of demo-up-showcase-load (create-user races the API's migrations, Phase 0 report Q3). local-dev's agent variable is CCF_AGENT_VERSION, not CCF_AGENT_IMAGE.
The docs-review-release prompt case became docs-review-verify (no rule dispatches docs-review with verifyAgainst any more).
